\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {35}{\ignorespaces Exhaustive routing of a succinct transition rule. Succinct representation exposes one charged derivation rather than a state-indexed policy table. The exact branch contains pure exact \(\mathsf  {Abs}\) and Geom on an exact quotient; the compensated branch contains reversible and general-resolvent quotient--Geom. The remaining support is identity-supported ambient Geom. In the ambient branch, control and reinforcement-learning terminology describes the represented kernel and selected generator; smooth, spectral, hierarchical, multiscale, or self-similar terminology describes the represented Geom data. These are not additional source channels. Only the authorized \(\mathsf  {Caus}\) component of the selected ambient current contributes directed structure; the remaining current is \(J_{\mathrm  {res}}\).}}{218}{figure.35}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig-succinct-transition-structural-routing}{{35}{218}{Exhaustive routing of a succinct transition rule. Succinct representation exposes one charged derivation rather than a state-indexed policy table. The exact branch contains pure exact \(\Abs \) and Geom on an exact quotient; the compensated branch contains reversible and general-resolvent quotient--Geom. The remaining support is identity-supported ambient Geom. In the ambient branch, control and reinforcement-learning terminology describes the represented kernel and selected generator; smooth, spectral, hierarchical, multiscale, or self-similar terminology describes the represented Geom data. These are not additional source channels. Only the authorized \(\Caus \) component of the selected ambient current contributes directed structure; the remaining current is \(\Res \)}{figure.35}{}}
\newlabel{fig-succinct-transition-structural-routing@cref}{{[figure][35][]35}{[1][217][]218}{}{}{}}
