\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {128}{\ignorespaces Walsh levels of the public hypercube. Eigenvalue \(2k/n\) grows with level, while multiplicity is binomial. The centered singleton spreads across all nonconstant levels, so placing a constant fraction in fast modes requires exponentially many active modes even though the singleton condenser capacity is only \(2^{-n}\). Bar heights are schematic.}}{619}{figure.128}\protected@file@percent }
